(; expect 0 ;)
(; Positive control: a rule whose typing constraint has no solution at all is sound, vacuously.  The
   left-hand side g b (mkB a) needs B a == C b, two distinct static heads: no instance is typable
   (confluence), so the rule never fires on a typable term.  Its right-hand side is typed by that
   constraint.  Dedukti refuses the rule (it cannot use a constraint it found unsatisfiable). ;)
A : Type.
B : A -> Type.
C : A -> Type.
mkB : a : A -> B a.

def g : b : A -> C b -> C b.
[a, b] g b (mkB a) --> mkB a.
